        "original_id": "31c5bcaf-245c-530f-b167-43ac7ff510aa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sigmund Jähn, Christer Fuglesang, Darin\n- Roles: cosmonaut, pilot, physicist, ESA astronaut\n- Organizations: ESA, Soviet Union Interkosmos programme\n- Events: first East German in space, STS-116, first Swedish citizen in space\n- Products: “Breathing Your Love” single\n\nFacts:\n- Sigmund Werner Paul Jähn was born on 13 February 1937.\n- Sigmund Jähn is a German cosmonaut and pilot.\n- In 1978, Sigmund Jähn became the first East German and the first German native to fly in space as part of the Soviet Union's Interkosmos programme.\n- Arne Christer Fuglesang was born on 18 March 1957 in Stockholm.\n- Christer Fuglesang is a Swedish physicist and an ESA astronaut.\n- On 10 December 2006 at 01:47 GMT, Christer Fuglesang was first launched aboard the STS-116 Space Shuttle mission.\n- Christer Fuglesang became the first Swedish citizen in space.\n- In October 2009, Christer Fuglesang took two copies of the single “Breathing Your Love” into space because his daughter was a Darin fan.\n- A photo of the “Breathing Your Love” disc with Earth in the distance is on Darin's official website.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
